8kloud-switcher (0.7.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add an SRT STREAM card to the console's OUTPUTS tab. It edits the
    transport (send on/off, listener/caller/rendezvous, host, port, latency
    in ms, passphrase and AES key length, stream id, any other FFmpeg srt
    option) and the encoding (HEVC/AV1, video and AAC bitrates, keyframe
    interval, NVENC preset and path). The fields fold into the one FFmpeg
    URL the show file stores and --srt-out takes, so existing show files
    keep working and a pasted URL fills the fields; SEND off parks the URL.
  * The encoder backend and preset, CLI-only until now, persist in the
    show file. New --srt-keyframe SEC and --srt-audio-bitrate KBPS flags on
    both executables; both NVENC backends take the keyframe interval.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:02:16 +0000

8kloud-switcher (0.7.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Quiet the libav errors every SRT connect logged while waiting for the
    first keyframe ("PPS id out of range", "Skipping invalid undecodable
    NALU", "Missing Sequence Header", for AV1 "No sequence header
    available"). A live stream is joined mid-GOP, so every packet until the
    keyframe is an error to a decoder and none of it is a fault. Both the
    stream probe and the decode loop up to the first picture now run under
    a per-thread quiet scope; decoder messages after that still show, and
    a failed probe logs its own warning.
  * Build the LGPL FFmpeg libraries with an $ORIGIN runpath instead of
    --enable-rpath, which wrote the build tree's absolute path into every
    library and into the pkg-config files, so the packaged binaries carried
    it too and preferred the build tree's copies on the machine that built
    them.
  * Link each executable with its final RPATH (KLOUD_PRIVATE_RPATH, set by
    debian/rules) instead of rewriting it at install time. The rewrite left
    dev binaries with an empty RPATH element, which ld.so reads as the
    current working directory. Package binaries now carry the private
    libdir alone.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:07:33 +0000

8kloud-switcher (0.7.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix AV1 SRT ingest and AV1 media clips decoding nothing since 0.7.2:
    enabling libdav1d made it FFmpeg's default AV1 decoder, and the SRT
    input took that default. libdav1d is software-only, ignores the CUDA
    device the input attaches, and cannot parse the draft AV1-in-MPEG-TS
    the SRT output sends, so the program went black while audio kept
    flowing. The input now picks the first decoder that accepts a CUDA
    hw_device_ctx (the native av1/hevc front ends on NVDEC) and falls
    back to FFmpeg's default only when none exists.
  * Add an ingest test that encodes HEVC and AV1 with NVENC, muxes each
    into the transport stream the SRT output sends, and plays it back
    through the SRT input on NVDEC; it fails without the fix.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:12:00 +0000

8kloud-switcher (0.7.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build the LGPL FFmpeg with libdav1d (BSD-2-Clause) so AV1 decodes in
    software where no NVDEC device is available. FFmpeg's native av1
    decoder is a hwaccel-only front end, so without it the AV1 program-
    output round-trip test failed and operator AV1 media needed a GPU.
  * Record the private FFmpeg's runtime dependencies (libsrt, gnutls,
    dav1d, zlib, bzip2, lzma) in Depends. They were previously never
    scanned, so the package installed cleanly on a fresh host and then
    failed to load. debian/shlibs.local keeps dpkg-shlibdeps from
    resolving the private libavcodec to the distribution's GPL build.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:47:07 +0000

8kloud-switcher (0.7.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Make libomt-c and the patched libvmx the default OMT runtime:
    packaging/build-omt.sh builds both from source into third_party/omt.
  * Pre-build VMX decoders for the show format at engine start and per
    input on patch (libomt-c's decoder pool), so a new 8K OMT connection's
    first frame arrives on time instead of 80 ms late with two dropped
    frames.
  * Document the libomt-c versus stock-libomt measurements at 1080p, 4K and
    8K in docs/omt.md.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:35:18 +0000

8kloud-switcher (0.7.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Replace the Qt desktop GUI with a web console served by 8kloud-switcher
    itself (default port 9924): the multiview streams to the browser as JPEG
    frames, and the WebSocket speaks the remote-control command language plus
    JSON commands for source patching, playlists and show settings.
  * Send the multiview wall over OMT with labels and tally rendered into the
    frame, on by default in the console (--no-mv-omt-out to disable).
  * Persist the show through a QSettings-compatible INI reader/writer, so an
    existing show.ini loads unchanged. Qt 6 is no longer a dependency.
  * Add an OUTPUTS tab for the restart-to-apply sender, SDI, SRT and bitrate
    settings, and a draggable monitor/deck split with selectable PGM/PVW
    layouts.
  * Fix the final show save running after engine stop, which emptied the
    stored input list on shutdown.

